From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:00:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: play silently instead of crashing when
 autoaudiosink is missing

createAutoAudioSink connected a signal to the result of creating
autoaudiosink without checking it, and MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer release-
asserts on the sink. autoaudiosink comes from gst-plugins-good, an optional
dependency, so on a system without it every page that creates a media
element crashed the web process.

Fall back to a fakesink with sync enabled, so media still plays at the right
pace without audio output. makeGStreamerElement already logs that the element
is missing.
---
 .../platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp        | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp
index 601837c7f917..f9fd788d59b1 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GStreamerCommon.cpp
@@ -1196,6 +1196,13 @@ bool gstElementFactoryEquals(GstElement* element, ASCIILiteral name)
 GstElement* /* (transfer floating) */ createAutoAudioSink(const String& role)
 {
     auto* audioSink = makeGStreamerElement("autoaudiosink"_s);
+    if (!audioSink) {
+        // autoaudiosink comes from gst-plugins-good. Without it, play silently rather than abort;
+        // sync keeps media paced to the clock.
+        audioSink = makeGStreamerElement("fakesink"_s);
+        g_object_set(audioSink, "sync", TRUE, nullptr);
+        return audioSink;
+    }
     g_signal_connect_data(audioSink, "child-added", G_CALLBACK(+[](GstChildProxy*, GObject* object, gchar*, gpointer userData) {
         auto* role = reinterpret_cast<StringImpl*>(userData);
         auto* objectClass = G_OBJECT_GET_CLASS(object);
